comments[2]:
  - created_at: "2026-08-03T20:56:39.512Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "A clean natural experiment, observed 2026-08-03 immediately after this item was filed.\n\nA commit touching only tracker data under the pm store, with no source, script, workflow or test file changed, turned the Windows regression job on main red. Two tests in the init command suite failed at 30010 and 30002 milliseconds, which is the generic Vitest timeout rather than an assertion. Re-running the failed job against byte-identical content passed, and main is green at the same commit.\n\nThe experiment is clean because the input could not have caused a behavioural change. Tracker data is not read by that suite, which sandboxes its own store path. So the failure carried zero information about the commit and the leg still reported red.\n\nTwo consequences for this item.\n\nFirst, the measured failure rate is a mixture and nothing separates its parts. Of the 28 alerts counted here, an unknown fraction are product defects that a pre-merge control would have caught, and an unknown fraction are infrastructure timeouts that no control can catch because there is nothing to catch. A rate that mixes them cannot justify any decision, which strengthens rather than weakens the case for measuring it properly: the first thing the meter has to do is partition.\n\nSecond, the timeout class is itself a recurrence. Two items in this tracker are already closed for the same subject, Windows init package acceptance exceeding the generic Vitest timeout, and both closed with a per-site timeout increase. The class has returned on a third site. That is the second independent recurrence found today and it arrived, unprompted, in the CI response to the commit that filed the recurrence work.\n\nPartitioning rule this suggests, recorded as input rather than as a decision: a failure whose signature is a timeout at the declared limit, on a leg whose median passing duration for that suite is far below the limit, and which passes on re-run with identical content, is infrastructure. Everything else is a candidate defect until proved otherwise. The re-run is the discriminator and it is cheap.\n"
  - created_at: "2026-10-03T12:05:39.807Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Fresh all-status intake: the strict corpus contains 2866 readable items, no omissions and only the three active receipt-correction owners in progress. Reuse this canonical nightly recurrence family rather than creating four duplicate occurrence items. Scheduled Nightly Validation run 37114037678 at ca6e718707d7a1582f7abc437f5bd88aab156dfd raised GH-1377 (Windows Node24 shard1: preview-snapshot invalid-lookup expected native ENOENT, received transaction_preview_snapshot_changed), GH-1378 (Windows Node24 shard2: search query cursor fingerprint mismatch plus settings entry/open race expectations), GH-1379 (Ubuntu Node22: three linked workspace-snapshot cases raise ENOENT during stat of dangling aliases), and GH-1380 (macOS Node24: settings entry/open race fallback and permission/link expectations). The Ubuntu Node24 coverage, independent quality and Ubuntu Node25 jobs passed; the four platform legs failed. These are real pre-existing-main observations distinct from PR1376 checks and source coverage. Historical shipped source lineages pm-5iwfkj, pm-gh1370 and pm-j668gl remain completed under their recorded boundaries; this recurrence intake records new platform investigation evidence, without claiming a repair or assigning inactive roadmap work. Each GitHub alert receives this canonical PM-file link and remains open pending independent platform repair proof."
    edited_at: "2026-10-03T12:20:41.253Z"
